pub const CHAPTER_6_PLAIN_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION: &str = "System Design\n\nProvide a detailed description of your software design using adequate diagrams and subsections as outlined below.\n\n## 6.1 System Use-Cases\n\nThis section outlines various use cases or scenarios that illustrate the key functionalities of the final system.\n\n## 6.2 Interaction Diagrams\n\nIllustrate the interactions between objects/classes using sequence or communication diagrams for different use case scenarios. You may exclude minor use cases. Include interaction diagrams for exceptional flows, which cover:\n\n- Error handling: Describe system responses to errors.\n- Time-out handling: Specify actions if a user does not respond within a set time.\n- Management of incorrect input: Address erroneous input for participating objects (e.g., incorrect user input).\n\n## 6.3 Class Diagram\n\nDefine all classes, including their attributes and methods. Highlight the interactions and relationships among these classes.\n\n## 6.4 System Architecture\n\nPresent the software architecture through diagrams and detailed descriptions.\n\n## 6.5 Database Design\n\nInclude a detailed entity-relationship diagram and corresponding schema, detailing the databases and file systems used in the project.\n\n## 6.6 User Interface Prototype\n\nProvide screenshots or mockups of the user interfaces to demonstrate the system's appearance and functionality in critical scenarios.\n\n## 6.7 Algorithms\n\nOffer a brief overview of any specialized algorithms used (e.g., image processing, game strategy, scheduling) and provide pseudo code for the system's major functionalities.\n";
